# F2 (MEASURE): fabric unicast x16 -> x4 with ttnn.point_to_point on the served (1, 4) mesh (scripts/ci/tp4_p2p_probe.py; docs/tp4-fabric-upload.md section 3).
# Arms: links and the relay pairs (fabric_upload_plan.relay_pairs), local (sender == receiver: the op's on-card copy ceiling), edges (every directed line edge at
# 256 MiB), far (0 -> 3, three hops), pairs (each x16 -> x4 pair alone at 4/64/256 MiB in ROW_MAJOR 16 KiB pages, TILE bfloat8_b and TILE bf16), both (the two pairs
# at once), reverse (x4 -> x16, the spill direction), relay (THE A/B: the one-coordinate host write re-checked, then the full relay - senders' own shards and the
# receivers' shards staged at the senders, point_to_point into the destination - against a direct write of the same bytes, per pair and all pairs, plus the production
# sharded write), socket (send_async/recv_async between (1, 1) submeshes, one and two connections: the multi-link path; last). Every transfer: first call timed apart,
# then timed calls into a preallocated output; exact = the receiver's shard equals the sender's bytes and every other shard keeps its sentinel.
# READ: 'P2P_PROBE verdict=MEASURED', its rates={...} (the per-pair GB/s decide() takes) and relay_over_direct={...} (under 0.8 on relay/*/all: the relay is faster).
# INEXACT = a transfer left bytes nobody wrote: the relay is NO-GO on that path. PARTIAL with 'relay arms skipped': the one-coordinate host write is not exact.
# Measurement only. The probe opens the mesh once and closes it; a hang ends at the probe's watchdog (exit 3, the report keeps the arms that finished) and the
# next job MUST reset all four cards (the ethernet-core wedge).
# TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the fabric-upload pack (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway
# commit of the branch and push the job's tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Names no rig, card, host or registry. ORDER.txt has the order, the minutes and every rule.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset fabric
C2_FABRIC_PROBE=p2p
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-11
